- op: discuss  # 8b52
  at: '2026-08-26T22:35:21Z'  # 8b52
  by: agent  # 8b52
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8b52
  clock: 3  # 8b52
  nonce: 8b52  # 8b52
  message: "SEQUENCING, recorded 2026-08-26 at the owner's request. THIS ITEM HAS NOW BEEN\nPUSHED BEHIND TWO SEPARATE ITEMS FOR THE SAME STRUCTURAL REASON, which is worth\nnoticing about the item itself and not just about its neighbours.\n\nThis item is the 5-name cap on the UNCATALOGUED-MODULE LIST: the cap is\n_MAX_REPORTED_UNCATALOGUED_MODULES = 5, the list is sorted(), so\nalphabetically-early stdlib names deterministically evict the third-party module\na reader could act on. Its own filing already notes that what INV-buzab changed\nwas that THE LIST GOT LONGER, which makes the eviction bite more often.\n\nThat is the tell: this item's severity is a FUNCTION OF THAT LIST'S LENGTH, so\nanything that changes the length changes the measurement.\n\n  INV-pusin (satisfied 2026-08-26, PR #556) SHORTENS it. Bare `std` and its\n  siblings were module_attr_ref ARTIFACTS of `use` statements, not calls at all.\n  Removing them removes entries from this list.\n\n  WI-tubij (cross-language clock rows) ALSO SHORTENS it. Adding catalogue rows\n  means more calls classify, so fewer modules are blamed for unclassified calls.\n\nMEASURING OR TUNING THIS ITEM BEFORE EITHER LANDS WOULD CALIBRATE A TRUNCATION\nAGAINST A DENOMINATOR THAT IS ABOUT TO SHRINK. The ranking rule its filing\nproposes -- third-party first, then alphabetical -- may still be right, but the\nEVIDENCE for how often eviction bites has to be re-derived on the post-fix list,\nnot the one measured in 2026-08.\n\nTHEREFORE: this item's position at stage 4 of the owner's arc\n(INV-pusin -> WI-lutuh + INV-zimud -> INV-vivok -> WI-fosir / INV-hosul -> P7)\nmay be too EARLY. Note that INV-hosul, its stage-4 partner, has no such\ndependency -- it is the opaque-launch caveat's doubled-name rendering, display\nonly, and nothing upstream changes its input. So the two halves of stage 4 are\nnot equally ready, and splitting them is a live option for the owner.\n\nNOT A STATUS CHANGE. This is sequencing information for whoever picks it up; the\nitem's own analysis of the defect is unaffected and still correct."  # 8b52
