  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-06 on dev f36a715bfb, at the owner's request, with the\nitem's OWN repro re-run live rather than the closing note re-read.\n\nFIXTURE: app/main.py imports 14 stdlib modules and calls requests.post;\napp/extra.py adds 9 more stdlib modules (bisect, calendar, colorsys, decimal,\ndifflib, fractions, graphlib, heapq, string) so the 5-name cap has to evict\nsomething. `hypergumbo verify-claims --claims\ndocs/example-claims/generic-taint-claims.yaml --no-default-overlays`, fresh\nXDG_CACHE_HOME:\n\n  could not classify (requests, calendar, colorsys, decimal,\n                      difflib.SequenceMatcher (+5 more))\n\n`requests` leads. Under the pre-fix plain sort the five shown would have been\nthe alphabetically-early stdlib names and `requests` would have been inside\n\"(+5 more)\" -- the filed defect. 14 tests in\ntest_verify_claims_disclosure_legibility.py pass through smart-test, mypy\nratchet clean.\n\nOBSERVED, NOT THIS ITEM: the gate now blames CALLS, not modules, so on the\noriginal 10-stdlib fixture only 3 names are unclassified today and the cap\nnever bites; it took 9 more uncatalogued modules to reach it. The fix is\nexercised less often than when filed, and still correct when it is.\n\nCLEANUP: removed the custom keys `status`, `priority`, `tags` that the create\nop had written through --field (INV-varil shape (a)); the top-level values\nwere already correct, so nothing about the item's state changed."  # b0d9
